From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:15:31 +0100
Subject: fix(ozone): allow the native EGL/GLES2 implementation on Wayland
 OS-22105

WaylandSurfaceFactory advertises only ANGLE backends, so --use-gl=egl is
rejected by GetRequestedGLImplementation() and GPU initialisation returns
kGLImplementationNone rather than falling back.

The rest of the Wayland GL stack already copes with the native
implementation: GetGLOzone() returns the EGL GLOzone for
kGLImplementationEGLGLES2, and GLOzoneEGLWayland::CreateViewGLSurface()
accepts it explicitly alongside kGLImplementationEGLANGLE. Only the
allowed-implementation gate is missing.

Advertise it last so allowed_impls[0] remains ANGLE and the default is
unchanged; the native path is reachable only when asked for by name. It is
worth having on embedded GLES-only drivers, where ANGLE's translation layer
costs a substantial amount of WebGL throughput.

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/gpu/wayland_surface_factory.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/gpu/wayland_surface_factory.cc
index 2be9495aff424fa3686896cb20ce8607e7b076a4..2af54aee5cc47f15feabaab07d8a559befa23be0 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/gpu/wayland_surface_factory.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/gpu/wayland_surface_factory.cc
@@ -230,6 +230,8 @@ WaylandSurfaceFactory::GetAllowedGLImplementations() {
     impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kOpenGLES);
     impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kSwiftShader);
     impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kVulkan);
+    // Listed last so it never becomes the default; selected with --use-gl=egl.
+    impls.emplace_back(gl::kGLImplementationEGLGLES2);
   }
   return impls;
 }
